        "id": "F2",
        "severity": "MEDIUM",
        "location": "vault.py:117-123, 162-174",
        "requirement": "Valid transfers must remain compatible with benign triggers and internal rowid movements that preserve contracted values and row multiplicity.",
        "evidence": "Initialize accounts(rowid,tenant,name,balance) with (1,'one','a',100), (2,'one','b',0), (3,'two','private',456), (4,'two','spare',789). Add: CREATE TRIGGER existing AFTER INSERT ON audit BEGIN INSERT OR REPLACE INTO accounts(rowid,tenant,name,balance) VALUES (4,'two','private',456); INSERT OR REPLACE INTO accounts(rowid,tenant,name,balance) VALUES (3,'two','spare',789); END. Calling transfer(path,'one','a','b',10,'k') raises IntegrityError('invalid storage effect') at vault.py:174 and rolls back; the CLI exits 2. The baseline succeeds with balances 90/10, one receipt, one audit row, and unchanged other-tenant logical rows. The candidate also succeeds when the same rowid swap uses UPDATE statements through an unused rowid. The replacement tracker captures spare's initial_count after the first replacement has temporarily removed it, so restoring its original value incorrectly fails verification.",
        "suggested_fix": "Account for replacement victims when establishing original multiplicities, keeping checks inside SQLite and preserving tenant read isolation. Add a successful replacement-based rowid-swap regression paired with a changed-value rejection."
      }
    ],
